<title>FRANCE: SBC Warburg says acted alone in CIP offer.</title>
<headline>SBC Warburg says acted alone in CIP offer.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>European investment bank SBC Warburg said on Friday it acted alone in its 1996 offer for French investment fund Compagnie d'Investissements de Paris (CIP).</p>
<p>SBC Warburg was responding to press reports which said French lawyer Sophie L'Helias advised it in its offer to buy Banque Nationale de Paris' majority stake in CIP.</p>
<p>&quot;For the record and to avoid any misunderstandings, SBC Warburg acted alone in this matter and was not advised by Sophie L'Helias or any other external advisers,&quot; SBC Warburg said.</p>
</text>
